# A synthetic card session: SELECT the ISD-R, then GetEUICCInfo2, then GetEID.
# The EUICCInfo2 and GetEuiccDataResponse DER below were produced by the
# generated encoder, not written by hand -- see testdata/cards/README.md for
# the program and the exact command that produced them. The STORE DATA
# framing around each ES10 request/response is hand-assembled, per
# rsp_es10.c's own citations (SGP.22 v2.6 5.7.2, GPCS 11.1.4/11.11.2).
#
# The SELECT exchange below is different: it is not assembled at all, it is
# copied byte-for-byte from a real probe against this project's own test
# eUICC over PC/SC at T=0 (fix round 2, Task 4's hardware access). Fix
# round 1's fixture had SELECT answer a bare 9000, which no real card with
# an FCI to return actually does -- this project's own card answers with
# '61 21' (33 more bytes waiting) and only gives up its FCI, AID and SGP.22
# version ('82 03 02 02 00' = "2.2.0") on the GET RESPONSE that follows.
# rsp_card_select_isdr silently returning "refused" on exactly this shape
# is the defect this fix round exists for; this fixture is what makes sure
# it cannot recur unnoticed. See testdata/cards/synthetic-info-direct-select.log
# for the other, less realistic shape (SELECT answering 9000 directly).

# SELECT the ISD-R AID (from the task brief):
# A0 00 00 05 59 10 10 FF FF FF FF 89 00 00 01 00
> 00 A4 04 00 10 A0 00 00 05 59 10 10 FF FF FF FF 89 00 00 01 00 00
< 6121

# GET RESPONSE for the 33 bytes '61 21' promised: the card's FCI ('6F'),
# carrying the DF name/AID back ('84 10 <AID>'), a proprietary template
# ('A5 04', holding '9F 65 01 FF'), and the eUICC's own SGP.22 version
# inside 'E0 05': '82 03 02 02 00' -- 2.2.0, the same version
# GetEUICCInfo2's svn reports below, from the same card.
> 00 C0 00 00 21
< 6F1F8410A0000005591010FFFFFFFF8900000100A5049F6501FFE0058203020200 9000

# GetEUICCInfo2Request ::= [34] SEQUENCE {} -- BF 22 00, one STORE DATA block
# (3 bytes fits well under the 255-byte limit, so P1 is the last-block form).
> 80 E2 91 00 03 BF 22 00 00
< BF226E810302010082030202008303060000840881020100820201008502000088020000A92C04140102030405060708090A0B0C0D0E0F10111213140414AABBCCDDEEFF11223344556677889900A1B2C3D4AA160414999897969594939291908988878685848382818004030201000C00 9000

# GetEuiccDataRequest ::= [62] SEQUENCE { tagList [APPLICATION 28] Octet1 }
# -- BF 3E 03 5C 01 5A, requesting the eidValue tag ('5A').
> 80 E2 91 00 06 BF 3E 03 5C 01 5A 00
< BF3E125A10890330121122334455667788990011FF 9000
